  "observationBoundary": "Seven cases replay the debug Map Test 0 prompt from one shared in-memory core state. A deterministic session-only copy of the verified ROM replaces the existing RunMapSetupInitFunction indirect call with a 16-byte FF-padding trampoline. The trampoline sets A6 to a RAM-owned three-word stream and JSRs one unmodified csc34_setBlocks or csc35_setBlocksVar handler; the original disk ROM is re-hashed unchanged before launch. Lua writes only the bounded FF0000 layout words, the update-toggle byte, and the input stream. It observes handler entry and return, the exact direct CopyMapBlocks call input, every copy instruction source/destination offset in order, the csc34 post-copy update-bit writes, and the exact layout readback window. It does not observe collision, pathfinding, story, save, visible VDP, or cycle timing effects. The original handlers and helper execute in one BizHawk launch.",
